    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="7.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Hu">Hu</ref> 7.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="7.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="194" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ se ðe ðone andagan brece — buton hit sy ðurh hlafordes geban —, gebete mid XXX scill', ⁊ to gesetton dæge gelæste þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he ær sceolde.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="7.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="194" ed="#liebermann"/>Et qui<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Hu_7-1.lnote.oe.6"/> terminum illum fregerit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Hu_7-1.lnote.oe.7"/> — nisi sit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Hu_7-1.lnote.oe.8"/> pro banno<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Hu_7-1.lnote.oe.9"/> domini uel infirmitate monstrabili<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Hu_7-1.lnote.oe.10"/> —, XXX sol. emendet, et ad constitutum diem faciat quod ante debuerat.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="7.1" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="195" ed="#liebermann"/>Qui illas inducias fregerit (quas<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Hu_7-1.lnote.oe.2"/> auctoritas totius centuriatus statuit), nisi sit propter edictum domini (sui<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Hu_7-1.lnote.oe.2"/>), emendet hoc XXX sol., et statuto termino (alio<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Hu_7-1.lnote.oe.3"/>) perficiat quod prius deberet.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="7.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="18" ed="#robertson"/>⁊ se ðe ðone andagan brece—buton hit sy ðurh hlafordes geban—gebete mid XXX scill', ⁊ to gesetton dæge gelæste þæt he ær sceolde.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="195" ed="#liebermann"/>Und wer diesen Termin bricht<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Hu_7-1.lnote.de.1"/> — ausser<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Hu_7-1.lnote.de.2"/> wenn es wegen Aufgebots durch [seinen] Herrn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Hu_7-1.lnote.de.3"/> geschieht —, büsse mit 30 Schill.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Hu_7-1.lnote.de.4"/> und leiste zum [neu] bestimmten Tage, was er vorher gesollt hätte.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And whoever breaks this term — unless it is because of a summons by [his] lord —, let him pay 30 shillings and perform on the [newly] appointed day what he should have done before.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="19" ed="#robertson"/>And he who fails to appear at the appointed time—unless prevented by a summons<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Hu_7-1.robnote.n.1"/> from his lord—shall pay 30 shillings<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#Hu_7-1.robnote.n.2"/> as compensation and perform on a fixed date what he should have done before.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="433" ed="#whitelock"/>And he who fails to appear on the appointed day—unless it is through his lord’s summons—to pay 30 shillings compensation, and on a fixed day perform what he should have done before.</ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hu_7-1.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">195</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">(<hi rend="italic">Glosse</hi>) <hi rend="italic">aus Hk; fehlt Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">(gloss) from Hk; lacking in Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hu_7-1.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">195</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">(<hi rend="italic">Glosse</hi>) <hi rend="italic">aus Hr; fehlt Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">(gloss) from Hr; lacking in Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hu_7-1.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">194</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">quin <hi rend="italic">Or</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">quin Or</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hu_7-1.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">194</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">infreg. <hi rend="italic">MHkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">infreg. MHkBr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hu_7-1.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">194</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt M</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in M</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hu_7-1.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">194</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">probando Deum <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">probando Deum K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hu_7-1.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">194</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">mostr. <hi rend="italic">R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">mostr. R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Hu_7-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">132</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Die Glosse zur Cons gehört nicht dieser, sondern einem Schreiber; denn Cons nennt das Hundred nie <hi rend="italic">centuriatus</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The gloss to Cons belongs not to Cons but to a scribe; for Cons never calls the hundred <hi rend="italic">centuriatus</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Hu_7-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">132</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Sunne 2 B.F, auch über Q's Einschiebung</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Sunne 2 B.F, also on Q's interpolation</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Hu_7-1.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">132</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Dienst des Königs in Heer oder Staat ist nicht der einzige hier gemeinte; das Gefolge (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 16i) wird vom Gesetz anerkannt als mögliches Hemmnis öffentlicher Bürgerpflicht</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The king’s service in the army or the state is not the only service meant here; the retinue (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 16i) is recognised by the law as a possible obstacle to the public duty of the citizen</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Hu_7-1.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">132</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. o</hi>. 5, 1¹; <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> Strafgeldfixum 5 (Z. 2 ff.). 8; Hundred 18</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. above</hi> 5, 1¹; <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> Strafgeldfixum 5 (l. 2 ff.). 8; Hundred 18</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Hu_7-1.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">301</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Probably for the carrying out of duties generally, cf. <hi rend="italic">hlafordes neod</hi> in the Law of the Cambridge Thanes (Thorpe, <hi rend="italic">Diplomatarium</hi>, p. 611). Q adds <hi rend="italic">vel infirmitate monstrabili</hi>, cf. <hi rend="italic">legerbære</hi> (<hi rend="italic">ibid.</hi>), and see P. and M. <hi rend="smallcaps">ii</hi>. pp. 562–3.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Hu_7-1.robnote.n.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">301</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">The regular fine payable to the hundred, cf. III Edm. 2; II Cn. 15, 2.</seg></note>
      </div>
